Chapter: HeapFrameReclaim
  cites Game chapter Rasterizer
  cites UI chapter Font
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Guards the shape the browser's event loop was given on 2026-08-11. That loop
 never returns, so on a bump allocator with no GC nothing it allocates is ever
 reclaimed by returning: it ran the heap from 6 MB to the guard page at
 0xb9e00000 and printed OUT OF MEMORY about two seconds after boot. The fix
 reclaims at two marks, and both halves are checked here.

 The frame half is the one that can fail SILENTLY, which is why it is measured
 by signature rather than by survival. Rendering inside a mark and restoring
 after the blit is only sound while nothing built during the render is still
 reachable afterwards; if that stops holding, the second render draws over
 memory the first one is still using and the pixels change while the program
 keeps running. Comparing every round against round one catches that, and the
 recorded signature has to be non-zero or a framebuffer that renders nothing
 at all would satisfy the comparison.

Section: Test

  fb-sum : Framebuf, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fb-sum (fb) (x) (y) (acc) =
    if y >= 7 then acc
    else if x >= 24 then fb-sum fb 0 (y + 1) acc
    else fb-sum fb (x + 1) y (acc + fb-get fb x y)

  frame-signature : Integer -> Integer
  frame-signature (ink) =
    let fb = fb-new 24 7 0
    in let drawn = font-draw-text fb font-5x7 "Hea" 0 0 ink 0
    in fb-sum drawn 0 0 0

  frame-rounds : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  frame-rounds (n) (expected) (bad) =
    if n <= 0 then bad
    else let mark = __heap-save
      in let sig = frame-signature 1
      in let reclaimed = __heap-restore mark
      in let sig-bad = if sig == expected then 0 else 1
      in let mark-bad = if __heap-save == mark then 0 else 1
      in frame-rounds (n - 1) expected (bad + sig-bad + mark-bad)

  idle-rounds : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  idle-rounds (n) (start) (bad) =
    if n <= 0 then bad
    else let mark = __heap-save
      in let junk = fb-new 8 8 3
      in let reclaimed = __heap-restore mark
      in idle-rounds (n - 1) start (bad + (if __heap-save == start then 0 else 1))

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let first = frame-signature 1
    in act
      print-line-uni (integer-to-text first)
      print-line-uni (integer-to-text (frame-rounds 5 first 0))
      print-line-uni (integer-to-text (idle-rounds 1000 __heap-save 0))
    end
  end
